  "query_preview": "/Friday through Tuesday/...\nIssued 201 PM MDT TUE AUG 4 2026\nA ridge of high pressure will \nremain over Utah on Friday and Saturday. Temperatures will be 5-10 \ndegrees above normal with lower valleys near 100 degrees Friday and \nSaturday. Monsoon moisture will reach far SE Oregon and southwest ID \nsouth of the Snake Basin on Friday afternoon. Current forecast does \nnot reflect this but there will be a slight chance of thunderstorms \nalong the NV border on Friday and Saturday afternoons. Westerly flow \nwill suppress the ridge on Sunday and Monday, bringing slightly \ncooler temperatures with dry and breezy conditions. Smoky conditions \nwill continue from area wildfires which may keep temperatures \nslightly cooler than forecast.",
